# Debian 12 (bookworm) golden image profile. PINNED TRUST ANCHORS (2026-11-15, agent AT; sources and cross-checks: docs/status/golden-image-results.md s1).
#
# FINDING: Debian does NOT publish a GPG signature for the current official cloud images (bookworm/latest has SHA512SUMS only, no SHA512SUMS.sign;
# cloud.debian.org/images/cloud/ itself says: "For the current official images ... the safest method is to download the image and checksum files over
# TLS ... DNSSEC"; only the legacy OpenStack/ directory carries SHA512SUMS.sign). A pin of a "Debian cloud image signing key" therefore does not exist
# and the old recipe's `fetch` could never have verified anything. The signed, authoritative anchor Debian DOES provide is the ARCHIVE: the golden
# image is built from the signed bookworm archive (mmdebstrap), whose Release files are verified against the pinned archive keys below.
UPSTREAM_MODE=bootstrap
DEBIAN_MIRROR=https://deb.debian.org/debian
DEBIAN_SECURITY_MIRROR=https://deb.debian.org/debian-security
DEBIAN_SUITE=bookworm
# Full fingerprints of the PRIMARY keys that may sign the bookworm Release files (both appear in ftp-master.debian.org/keys.html AND in the
# debian-archive-keyring 2023.4 package AND are what the live InRelease/Release.gpg of bookworm verify against, checked 2026-11-15):
#   B8B8 0B5B 623E AB6A D877 5C45 B7C5 D7D6 3509 47F8  Debian Archive Automatic Signing Key (12/bookworm)
#   4D64 FEC1 19C2 0290 67D6 E791 F8D2 585B 8783 D481  Debian Stable Release Key (12/bookworm)
#   05AB 9034 0C0C 5E79 7F44 A8C8 254C F3B5 AEC0 A8F0  Debian Security Archive Automatic Signing Key (12/bookworm)
ARCHIVE_KEY_FPRS="B8B80B5B623EAB6AD8775C45B7C5D7D6350947F8 4D64FEC119C2029067D6E791F8D2585B8783D481 05AB90340C0C5E797F44A8C8254CF3B5AEC0A8F0"
ARCHIVE_KEY_FILES="debian-archive-bookworm-automatic.asc debian-archive-bookworm-stable.asc debian-archive-bookworm-security-automatic.asc"
